<article class="env-lemma" id="07NV">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07NV">Lemma <span data-tag="07NV">15.44.1</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a Noetherian local ring. Then $\dim (A) = \dim (A^\wedge )$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/031C" data-tag="031C">10.97.4</a> the map $A \to A^\wedge $ induces isomorphisms $A/\mathfrak m^ n = A^\wedge /(\mathfrak m^\wedge )^ n$ for $n \geq 1$. By Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/02M0" data-tag="02M0">10.52.12</a> this implies that 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \text{length}_ A(A/\mathfrak m^ n) = \text{length}_{A^\wedge }(A^\wedge /(\mathfrak m^\wedge )^ n)  \]
</div>
    <p>
       for all $n \geq 1$. Thus $d(A) = d(A^\wedge )$ and we conclude by Algebra, Proposition <a href="/tag/00KQ" data-tag="00KQ">10.60.9</a>. An alternative proof is to use Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00ON" data-tag="00ON">10.112.7</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>